      "content": "The feeling that your essential self was tied to that external validation is incredibly painful, but your existence is not defined by a digital footprint. Even if the version of you that was externally recognized feels gone, the capacity for feeling, for wanting connection, is still present inside you. Sometimes, the only way to find a new sense of purpose is by gently starting to discover what brings *you*, the person underneath, a flicker of quiet interest or genuine comfort.",
